# DRETH TODO

This file is the operational source of truth. Items are ordered by dependency.
Do not implement a later item before its prerequisites are done.
Do not claim an item is done unless its acceptance tests pass.

---

## What the code currently does vs what the taxonomy requires

The taxonomy (DRETH_TAXONOMY.md) defines claims scoped to named operations with
explicit authority and stored scope records. The code has:

- one unscoped string per variable: `operation_role = "tareth" | "trass"`
- no named operation on the claim
- no authority field
- no scope record
- `_certify_form_role` running every cycle regardless of triggers
- no `predict_under_joint_intervention`
- no joint false-trass test

The gap is not cosmetic. The taxonomy's core rule — `trass-for-skip` does not
imply `trass-for-route` — is not expressible in the current code. The same
`operation_role` value gates skip, parent selection, routing, form shortcuts,
and compression simultaneously. That is wrong.

---

## Known drift risks — read before implementing anything

These are the exact places implementation will silently revert to pattern-matching
if not actively prevented. Each has a constraint added to the relevant step below.

**DRIFT 1 — Cosmetic migration in T1 (most likely failure):**
`role_for("skip")` falls back to `operation_role` when no cert exists. It is
possible to migrate all gate syntax — replace `n.operation_role == "trass"` with
`n.role_for("skip") == "trass"` — and call T1 done while nothing actually changed.
The taxonomy's core rule (`trass-for-skip ≠ trass-for-route`) remains inexpressible
for vars because only forms get route certs in T1. Vars never get separate skip vs
route verdicts. The structure looks right. The semantics are not there.
CONSTRAINT: T1 is not done until a test asserts a var has `role_for("skip") ==
"tareth"` and `role_for("route") == "untested"` simultaneously. Two different values.
If no test asserts this, T1 is not done.

**DRIFT 2 — T2.1 "design documentation only" is morphology:**
A comment that nothing reads is the same as no implementation. T2.1 as a standalone
step will be marked complete after adding a comment block. That comment changes
nothing.
CONSTRAINT: T2.1 is deleted as a standalone step. The documentation lives as
inline comments inside the `invalidate()` method in T2.2. If the method does not
exist, the documentation does not exist.

**DRIFT 3 — `keep_skip_cert=True` in T2.2 will never be called:**
The invalidate method as specified includes a `keep_skip_cert=True` path for when
the caller has verified downstream structure is unchanged. There is no infrastructure
to verify that. The conservative path always runs. The untangling is fake — the skip
cert gets flagged on every parent change just like `operation_role` did before.
CONSTRAINT: Remove `keep_skip_cert` from T2.2 entirely. The correct behavior is:
parent change flags skip cert as untested (requiring retest), not clears it. That is
sufficient and honest. Do not add a parameter that will never be called with True.

**DRIFT 4 — T3.1 fourth trigger site will be skipped:**
Four trigger sites are named for `needs_role_retest = True`. The fourth — "when any
instance's parent set changes" — is hard to wire because parent changes are per-var,
not per-form-instance. The first three (bind, unbind, quarantine recovery) will be
wired and the fourth will be silently dropped.
CONSTRAINT: T3.1 requires a test that changes an instance's parents mid-run and
asserts `_certify_form_role` fires on the next cycle. Without that test, the fourth
trigger is not done and T3.1 is not done.

**DRIFT 5 — T4's `_is_ancestor` uses agent hypothesis, not truth:**
`_is_ancestor(a, b)` walks the ledger's known parent structure — what the agent
believes, not the true causal structure. If the agent has a wrong hypothesis, the
joint test trigger silently fails to fire in exactly the cases where it matters most.
CONSTRAINT: Document this as an explicit known limitation inside `_test_joint_false_trass`.
The T4.2 acceptance test must use a world where the agent has the correct hypothesis,
so the trigger fires. Do not write a test that passes only because the trigger is
bypassed.

**DRIFT 7 — Var route certs are never created; core rule is half-implemented after T5:**
After all T0–T5 steps are complete, `trass-for-skip ≠ trass-for-route` is real
for forms, fake for vars. Vars use skip cert as proxy for route eligibility
throughout T1.4. No T step creates var route certs. The T1.3 drift guard tests
object isolation — it cannot catch this because it only constructs a synthetic
VarNethra, not a real agent run.
CONSTRAINT: Do not claim the taxonomy's core rule is fully implemented after T5.
Claim: "implemented for forms; vars use skip-as-route proxy until D5." This must
be stated in the T5 acceptance text, not buried in T1.4.

**DRIFT 8 — T2.3 event classification is a judgment call that will be wrong:**
There are ~15 direct `operation_role` assignments in agent.py. T2.3 says "determine
which event caused it" — left to implementation-time judgment. Misclassifying one
(e.g. structural_mutation where parent_change is correct) silently changes the cert
cascade. No test catches wrong event type unless tests explicitly assert cert state
after each event.
CONSTRAINT: T2.3 requires classifying every site before touching any code. See
the site classification table in T2.3. Tests must check cert key state, not just
the final operation_role string.

**DRIFT 9 — T4.3 "after quarantine events" has no single location in code:**
Quarantine events are set in multiple paths across agent.py. Wiring
`_find_joint_trass_candidates` to only one path silently misses others.
CONSTRAINT: Track quarantines-this-cycle in `self._quarantined_this_cycle`.
Clear it at the start of `run_cycle`. Every path that sets `n.status =
"quarantined"` adds to it. Call `_find_joint_trass_candidates` once at the END
of `run_cycle`. This is the only location. See T4.3 for exact wiring.

**DRIFT 10 — VarNethra.invalidate() name collision with ChainedLedger.invalidate():**
ChainedLedger.invalidate(vars, cycle, reason) already exists at ledger.py:525.
T2.2 adds VarNethra.invalidate(event) — same name, different object. During T2.3
the grep output will show ledger.invalidate(...) calls at lines 1248 and 1462.
These must NOT be replaced with n.invalidate_certs(event) — they cascade status
through descendants which is separate from cert invalidation.
CONSTRAINT: T2.2's method must be named `invalidate_certs(event)` not
`invalidate(event)`. Every reference in T2.2, T2.3, T3.2 must use that name.

**DRIFT 11 — Line 873 false-trass contradiction has no event type in T2.2:**
agent.py:873: `pn.operation_role = "untested"` is the false-trass contradiction
path — a child var picked a trass parent, contradiction detected. This is NOT
"parent_change", "sentinel_failure", or "drift". T2.2's invalidate_certs() has
no event for this. T2.3 "classify each site" gives no guidance on this line.
CONSTRAINT: T2.2 must add event type "false_trass_contradiction" with behavior:
flag skip cert as untested (same as sentinel_failure). T2.3 must explicitly name
line 873 as the one site that uses this event type.

**DRIFT 12 — Sentinel failure path never resets operation_role — T3.2 must ADD, not replace:**
ledger.py:525 ChainedLedger.invalidate() resets n.status (certified→uncertain)
but NEVER touches n.operation_role. After sentinel failure at agent.py:1462,
operation_role remains "tareth". There is no scattered assignment to replace.
T3.2 must ADD `n.invalidate_certs("sentinel_failure")` after the existing
ledger.invalidate() call — it is not replacing anything. The TODO currently
implies T3.2 is replacing an existing assignment. That is wrong.

**DRIFT 13 — T4.3 trigger "quarantined vars" — var status never becomes "quarantined":**
Var n.status goes to "uncertain" after sentinel failure (see ledger.py:543).
n.status = "quarantined" does not exist for VarNethra. Only form.health_status
becomes "quarantined" (forms.py:902, 983). The trigger `_quarantined_this_cycle`
tracking `n.status == "quarantined"` will always be empty — the condition never
fires. The correct trigger is: vars that transitioned to n.status == "uncertain"
due to sentinel failure this cycle. Rename to `_uncertain_this_cycle`. Populate
it in both places where sentinel failure cascades: agent.py:1462 (main loop)
and agent.py:1248 (dormant safety sweep). These are the only two sites.

**DRIFT 6 — T5 will be deferred indefinitely (fatal):**
Removing the legacy `operation_role` field is the proof that T0–T4 actually worked.
It is also the hardest and most frightening step. It will be deferred. The certs will
become a parallel structure nobody is forced to use. `operation_role` will remain the
true decision field forever.
CONSTRAINT: T5 is the acceptance test for T0–T4. If T5 cannot be completed, T0–T4
are not done. The legacy field removal is not a cleanup step. It is the proof. Add
this statement to T5 explicitly.

